{"entryId":"1168","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1168:1","sourceSha256":"bea8e04914b974609e4e89b77dcdcb7ea760972b0a9a8cd143017a81162e904c","englishSha256":"a2ba62acf12c06ab6a01830668f8531eee1d172220322cfba5f0d050a2bfbb2b","citations":[{"id":"1168:1:citation-01","he":[42,65],"en":[72,93],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_54b.20"},"reference":"Shabbat 54b:20","assessment":"Several Moed witnesses attest the cluster. Shabbat and Megillah explicitly attach a Yochanan/Yonatan substitution statement to the formula. The parenthetical means see there.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 54b:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_54b.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Megillah 7a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_7a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sukkah 4b:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sukkah_4b.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1168:1:citation-02","he":[66,96],"en":[130,141],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_51a.9"},"reference":"Chullin 51a:9","assessment":"The two sages discuss an animal in Chaviva’s household. Neither passage resolves this Chaviva against other bearers.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 51a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_51a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1168:1:citation-03","he":[253,282],"en":[369,417],"target":{"entry":1173,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1173:1","assessment":"The candidate is Rav Yosef’s son in the nearby entry and its Bava Batra attestation. The link is a pointer at most and the identification is conjectural.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1173:1","target":{"entry":1173,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Bava Batra 143b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_143